NEARS-3535 — regression sweep evidence (contract-unchanged checks)

apiGuestCheck middleware still rejects invalid guest_id/token combos with 401, same as before:
  - wrong X-Guest-Token for a real guest_id -> HTTP 401 {"errors":"Unauthorized"}
    ([FAIL] guest.token.rejected reason=token_mismatch)
  - guest_id belonging to another guest ("ride" attempt, see AC1/AC2 log) -> HTTP 401
    (reason=token_mismatch)
  - legacy null-token guest under strict (default) -> HTTP 401 (reason=legacy_null_token_strict)

place_order / prescription_place_order contract unchanged (200/403, never 500):
  - POST /api/v1/customer/order/place with missing required fields (authenticated user) ->
    HTTP 403 with standard validator error payload (order_type/store_id/distance/address/... )
  - POST /api/v1/customer/order/prescription/place with missing required fields -> HTTP 403
    with standard validator error payload (payment_method/store_id/.../order_attachment)

Non-buy-now placement path untouched by the buy-now-only idempotency gate:
  Authenticated user (id=6), same X-Idempotency-Key
  (11111111-2222-3333-4444-555566667777) submitted twice with is_buy_now=0:
    1st: HTTP 200, order_id=91809 (orders count 52 -> 53)
    2nd (same key): HTTP 200, order_id=91810 (orders count 53 -> 54)
  -> TWO distinct orders placed, confirms the buy-now gate never engages on the non-buy-now path
     (matches BuyNowOrderIdempotencyTest::test_non_buy_now_placement_ignores_idempotency_header_and_is_never_gated).

